The Android NDK defines timezone_t but not the related types and functions
gnulib expects to come with it, and gnutls assumes that finding timezone_t
means having all of them.  This stops configure from detecting timezone_t and
renames gnulib's own timezone_t to rpl_timezone_t so the two do not collide.

Every declaration and definition of the type has to be renamed together: the
NDK's timezone_t is a different type, so leaving one behind is a compile error
rather than something that quietly works.  Check for stragglers with

    grep -rn '\btimezone_t\b' src/gl/ | grep -v rpl_timezone_t

after a gnutls version bump, because gnulib moves this code around: 3.8.13
added an _GL_FUNCDECL_RPL declaration of tzfree and gave the definition in
time_rz.c an errno-preserving wrapper, neither of which existed when this
patch was first written.

